		label: 'Get query results',
		description: 'Returns the results of a query job.',
		context:
			'---\nname: getQueryResults\ndescription: Returns the results of a query job.\n---\n\nFetches the results of a query job started by the runQuery or createJob endpoint. Pass the `jobId` from `jobReference.jobId` and, for jobs outside the `US` and `EU` multi-regions, the job\'s `location`.\n\nWhen `jobComplete` is `false` the job is still running and no rows are returned; call again (the call waits up to `timeoutMs`, default 10,000 ms). Rows use the cell format described by `schema.fields`: `{ "f": [ { "v": value }, ... ] }` per row. Timestamp cells are floating-point seconds unless `useInt64Timestamp` or `timestampOutputFormat` is set (at most one of the two; the API rejects both together).\n\nPaging: `maxResults` sizes the page, `startIndex` jumps to a zero-based row, and `pageToken` from the previous response continues the listing. `totalRows` is the full result size.\n\nReference: [jobs.getQueryResults](https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest/v2/jobs/getQueryResults).\n',
